WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:12.640
73. The Wild Amazon. Step inside, and the air is rich and heavy, full of oxygen that

2
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.600
the plants breathe out. Everything is green. The light comes down through the leaves of

3
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:25.560
the trees high above. Growing things pile on top of each other. Vines on trees, moss

4
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:33.560
on vines, fungi and flowers everywhere. Animals large and small hide in the tangled plants.

5
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:40.600
It seems quiet, but the air is actually full of the sound of leaves and insects moving.

6
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:47.160
This is the Amazon rainforest. The Amazon rainforest covers most of the Amazon basin

7
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.160
of South America. It covers five and a half million square kilometers, mostly in Brazil,

8
00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:00.440
but reaching into some other countries as well. It is ancient, at least fifty-five million

9
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:07.880
years old. It is full of fresh water from its many rivers. The Amazon rainforest has

10
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:13.960
the most animal and plant species in one place in the world. One in ten living species of

11
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:20.960
plants or animals make their home in the Amazon. One in five of all birds live in the Amazon.

12
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:28.200
It is incredibly rich, and we have discovered and documented only a small part of it. That

13
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:35.200
is why the destruction of the Amazon is so frightening and so serious. Deforestation,

14
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.920
cutting down forests for farming or pasture, is a major threat. Though the deforestation

15
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:49.160
rate has slowed, the Amazon still loses many miles of forest every year. For every mile

16
00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:55.520
lost, we may lose valuable plants and animals. We also depend on the plants in the Amazon

17
00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:02.520
for oxygen. Killing them may accelerate global warming. The Amazon is one of the world's

18
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:09.760
few remaining wild, mysterious places. Let's protect it before it's too late.
